and not due to willful neglect, and, for our taxable year ended December 31, 2004, we attach to our U.S. federal income tax return a schedule of the sources of our income, and any incorrect information on the schedule was not due to fraud with
intent to evade tax. For all subsequent taxable years, we are not required to attach a schedule to our U.S. federal income tax return on an annual basis, but rather are only required to file such a schedule in the taxable year in which such failure
is identified. It is not possible to state whether we would be entitled to the benefit of these relief provisions in all circumstances. If these relief provisions are inapplicable to a particular set of circumstances involving us, we will not
